let's:
We do' want stragglers a-layin' 'roun' hyeah;
Let's gin him 'way to de big buggah-man;
I know he's hidin' erroun' hyeah right neah.

letting:
To the blue luminous tremor of the air,
And letting drop the white wax as they went
To eat the bishop’s wafer at the church;

lethargy:
So, when you had risen
from all the lethargy of love and its heat,
you would have summoned me,

lettice:
Reaping one, reaping all.
Sing pretty Lettice,
Sing Rachel, sing May;

letter's:
Explaining all but the explanation;
As if we a ciphered letter’s cipher hit
And find it in an unknown language writ.
